    "summary": "Traditional web onboarding is modeled as presentation bindings over canonical actions and scenarios. The first evidence-backed bindings cover password registration, email verification, and invitation review with concrete routes, view IDs, fields, semantic finders, operations, and expected views. Composite registration behavior and legacy invitation navigation are recorded as implementation seams rather than alternate authentication rules. Next major area: Section 4.13, Session projection and routing."
